{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>וַיַּקְהֵל עֲלֵיהֶם</b> ['and he assembled against them']. That is, they did not assemble of their own will, but Korah assembled them. Accordingly, the verse declares the praise of the congregation. Or it may intend to give a reason for the statement of HaShem that comes afterward: <b>הִבָּדְלוּ מִתּוֹךְ הָעֵדָה</b> etc. <b>וַאֲכַלֶּה אוֹתָם</b> — and the objector would say: if Korah and his company sinned, why should these sheep perish? Therefore He prefaced and said that they assembled by Korah's desire and for his love, and therefore they appear to be willing participants in his deed, and therefore HaShem said: הִבָּדְלוּ etc. וַאֲכַלֶּה אוֹתָם." "<b>וַיֵּרָא כְבוֹד ה׳</b> ['and the glory of HaShem appeared']. His Shekhinah, may He be blessed, was revealed to the entire congregation, so that they would recognize that He is the one who executes written judgment, and that He is the one who selects who is fit to minister before Him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:15.300545061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}